1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,100
What if, right now… you could see exactly what

2
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:05,600
was going to happen in the next 10 seconds?

3
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:09,433
What would you do? Avoid an embarrassing fall?

4
00:00:10,333 --> 00:00:14,200
Prevent an accident? Find out what your crush is about to say?

5
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:17,300
Or… use those 10 seconds to change something

6
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:19,800
you might regret for the rest of your life?

7
00:00:20,733 --> 00:00:23,133
It sounds like a pretty small superpower.

8
00:00:24,033 --> 00:00:28,100
But think about it. Ten seconds can sometimes change everything.

9
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:33,767
The rule is simple. Whenever you focus and blink…

10
00:00:34,167 --> 00:00:37,300
you can see exactly 10 seconds into the future.

11
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:39,833
Not a feeling. Not a prediction.

12
00:00:40,233 --> 00:00:42,733
You actually see what is about to happen.

13
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:44,833
Then… you return to the present.

14
00:00:45,267 --> 00:00:48,667
And you have 10 seconds to decide: let that future happen…

15
00:00:49,067 --> 00:00:50,300
or try to change it.

16
00:00:50,700 --> 00:00:53,433
At first? You would obviously use this incredible

17
00:00:53,433 --> 00:00:56,200
power for the most important things in life.

18
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:58,567
Like… not embarrassing yourself.

19
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:02,867
You see yourself trip. And somehow…

20
00:01:03,467 --> 00:01:06,667
the entire cup of coffee ends up all over your clothes.

21
00:01:07,267 --> 00:01:10,767
Even worse… someone nearby is already holding a phone.

22
00:01:11,367 --> 00:01:14,567
No. The internet does not need another meme today.

23
00:01:15,167 --> 00:01:16,867
You return to the present.

24
00:01:17,433 --> 00:01:19,233
Step slightly to the left.

25
00:01:19,833 --> 00:01:23,167
Avoid the crack. Perfect. You smile confidently.

26
00:01:23,767 --> 00:01:26,133
Having a superpower feels amazing.

27
00:01:26,733 --> 00:01:28,800
Then… you walk straight into a pole.

28
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:33,367
BONK! Apparently… seeing the future still cannot save your dignity.

29
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:39,000
During a meeting… you suddenly see your boss calling your name.

30
00:01:39,100 --> 00:01:41,167
You have exactly 10 seconds.

31
00:01:41,233 --> 00:01:44,067
Your brain instantly enters emergency mode.

32
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:47,433
You open the document. Scan the most important line.

33
00:01:47,533 --> 00:01:50,767
Ten seconds later… “What do you think?” You sit up straight.

34
00:01:50,867 --> 00:01:54,100
Stay calm. And give a surprisingly intelligent answer.

35
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:57,067
Everyone nods. Your boss looks impressed.

36
00:01:57,167 --> 00:02:02,133
Congratulations. You just used a supernatural ability to look like someone…

37
00:02:02,267 --> 00:02:05,067
who was actually paying attention during the meeting.

38
00:02:05,167 --> 00:02:08,900
And honestly… that might be one of the best uses of this power.

39
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:13,933
Sometimes the power would help with much smaller things.

40
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:17,133
You see your phone about to fall off the table.

41
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:19,300
The screen hits the floor.

42
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:22,000
Shatters. You return to the present.

43
00:02:22,467 --> 00:02:24,233
Calmly reach out your hand.

44
00:02:24,700 --> 00:02:26,600
The cat pushes the phone.

45
00:02:27,067 --> 00:02:28,933
And… you catch it. Perfect.

46
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:33,567
Your superpower just saved you a few hundred dollars in repairs.

47
00:02:34,033 --> 00:02:35,633
But from this point on…

48
00:02:36,100 --> 00:02:38,467
things start getting much more serious.

49
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:42,633
You are about to cross the street.

50
00:02:43,567 --> 00:02:46,933
The light is green. Everything looks completely normal.

51
00:02:47,867 --> 00:02:49,700
Then you blink. And see…

52
00:02:50,633 --> 00:02:53,167
a vehicle speeding out from a blind corner.

53
00:02:54,100 --> 00:02:56,533
If you keep moving… you are going to collide.

54
00:02:57,467 --> 00:02:59,000
You return to the present.

55
00:02:59,967 --> 00:03:02,600
And stop. One second. Two seconds.

56
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:06,467
Three. The vehicle actually flies past you.

57
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:09,233
Only a few feet away.

58
00:03:10,167 --> 00:03:11,800
And for the first time…

59
00:03:12,700 --> 00:03:14,933
you realize something. This power is

60
00:03:14,933 --> 00:03:17,533
not just useful for avoiding embarrassing moments.

61
00:03:18,467 --> 00:03:20,067
It could save your life.

62
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:22,967
Maybe even someone else’s.

63
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:28,600
And of course… you would immediately think about sports.

64
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:32,333
During a game… you see your opponent move to the right.

65
00:03:33,133 --> 00:03:35,400
Easy. You return to the present…

66
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:39,000
and move right before he even makes his move.

67
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:41,267
But there is a problem.

68
00:03:42,067 --> 00:03:45,000
He sees you move. So he changes direction.

69
00:03:45,833 --> 00:03:48,367
Left. Wait. That is not what you saw.

70
00:03:49,167 --> 00:03:52,633
And that is when you discover the biggest problem with your power.

71
00:03:53,433 --> 00:03:55,200
The future is not fixed.

72
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,267
The moment you change what you do…

73
00:03:59,067 --> 00:04:03,167
the future changes too. Every decision creates a different outcome.

74
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:08,700
During a job interview… you see the next question.

75
00:04:10,200 --> 00:04:13,900
“What is your biggest weakness?” You have 10 seconds to prepare.

76
00:04:15,433 --> 00:04:17,567
This time… no awkward silence.

77
00:04:19,033 --> 00:04:21,733
No panic. You deliver the perfect answer.

78
00:04:23,267 --> 00:04:27,200
The interviewer smiles. But then you look 10 seconds ahead again.

79
00:04:28,667 --> 00:04:32,100
And hear him ask: “Did you prepare that answer beforehand?” …

80
00:04:33,633 --> 00:04:37,533
Okay. Maybe this power cannot save you from every interview.

81
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:42,633
But some things are much harder.

82
00:04:42,867 --> 00:04:46,167
You are standing in front of someone you have liked for months.

83
00:04:46,467 --> 00:04:49,233
The words have been stuck in your head forever.

84
00:04:49,467 --> 00:04:51,700
You blink. And see her reaction.

85
00:04:51,967 --> 00:04:53,833
“I’m sorry…” Your heart drops.

86
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:55,633
Now you have a choice.

87
00:04:55,900 --> 00:04:58,200
You could stay silent. Say nothing.

88
00:04:58,467 --> 00:05:01,367
Never get rejected. Never feel the pain.

89
00:05:01,633 --> 00:05:03,400
But then you start thinking…

90
00:05:03,667 --> 00:05:06,433
if you avoid every future you do not like…

91
00:05:06,667 --> 00:05:09,167
are you really living? You take a breath.

92
00:05:09,433 --> 00:05:12,833
And say it anyway. “I like you.” She pauses.

93
00:05:13,100 --> 00:05:15,533
Then… “I’m sorry. I’m just not ready

94
00:05:15,533 --> 00:05:17,967
for a relationship.” Exactly what you saw.

95
00:05:18,233 --> 00:05:19,933
But this time… you smile.

96
00:05:20,167 --> 00:05:22,467
Because at least now… you have an answer.

97
00:05:22,767 --> 00:05:25,267
Some futures do not need to be changed.

98
00:05:25,500 --> 00:05:28,633
Sometimes… you just need enough courage to face them.

99
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:33,767
Then one day… those 10 seconds really change you.

100
00:05:33,900 --> 00:05:36,500
Your phone starts ringing. It is your mom.

101
00:05:36,667 --> 00:05:39,267
You are busy. You think: “I’ll call her

102
00:05:39,267 --> 00:05:42,167
back later.” Your finger moves toward the decline button.

103
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:45,467
But out of habit… you look 10 seconds into the future.

104
00:05:45,633 --> 00:05:47,867
You see yourself rejecting the call.

105
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:50,500
Walking forward. And behind you…

106
00:05:50,667 --> 00:05:53,133
an elderly man steps into the road.

107
00:05:53,267 --> 00:05:55,433
A truck is coming straight toward him.

108
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:57,233
You return to the present.

109
00:05:57,367 --> 00:05:59,567
You do not think. You run.

110
00:05:59,700 --> 00:06:02,000
Grab the man. Pull him backward.

111
00:06:02,167 --> 00:06:05,667
The truck flies past. Missing both of you by inches.

112
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:10,133
You are breathing hard. The man does not even understand what just happened.

113
00:06:10,300 --> 00:06:12,400
You just saved someone’s life.

114
00:06:12,533 --> 00:06:14,433
Then… your phone vibrates again.

115
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:16,333
Your mom is still calling.

116
00:06:16,433 --> 00:06:19,367
You answer. “Mom?” There is a brief silence.

117
00:06:19,500 --> 00:06:22,900
Then she simply asks: “Did you eat yet?” That is it.

118
00:06:23,033 --> 00:06:25,600
No emergency. No terrible news.

119
00:06:25,767 --> 00:06:29,367
No dramatic final words. Just an ordinary question.

120
00:06:29,500 --> 00:06:32,133
The kind of question you might ignore every day.

121
00:06:32,267 --> 00:06:36,733
You laugh. “Yeah, Mom. I already ate.” You talk for a few minutes.

122
00:06:36,867 --> 00:06:39,633
Nothing dramatic happens. But suddenly…

123
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:42,200
you realize something. You spent the entire

124
00:06:42,200 --> 00:06:44,567
day staring 10 seconds into the future…

125
00:06:44,700 --> 00:06:47,467
and nearly ignored someone who was with you…

126
00:06:47,633 --> 00:06:48,600
right now.

127
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:52,900
You thought the greatest part of your power…

128
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,133
was knowing what would happen next.

129
00:06:57,200 --> 00:07:01,133
But it was not. Because even if you can see 10 seconds ahead…

130
00:07:02,233 --> 00:07:05,267
you still do not know what happens in 10 minutes.

131
00:07:06,367 --> 00:07:10,300
Tomorrow. Next year. Or when the last time you see someone…

132
00:07:11,400 --> 00:07:13,800
will actually be. And maybe…

133
00:07:14,900 --> 00:07:17,933
that is exactly what gives life its meaning.

134
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:23,133
Of course… seeing 10 seconds into the future is only

135
00:07:23,133 --> 00:07:25,933
a thought experiment. It is not something we can actually do.

136
00:07:25,967 --> 00:07:29,400
In real life… there is no rewind button. No warning screen. No countdown

137
00:07:29,400 --> 00:07:32,800
telling us that an important moment is about to happen. But maybe… we

138
00:07:32,800 --> 00:07:36,233
do not need one. You can still look before crossing the street. You

139
00:07:36,233 --> 00:07:39,400
can still say what you really feel. You can call your parents.

140
00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:42,833
Apologize to someone. Thank someone. Hold someone you love for a little longer.

141
00:07:42,833 --> 00:07:46,233
And sometimes… small decisions like those are enough to change the future. You

142
00:07:46,233 --> 00:07:49,667
do not need to see 10 seconds ahead to live a better life.

143
00:07:49,700 --> 00:07:52,867
You just need to stop wasting… the 10 seconds you have right

144
00:07:52,867 --> 00:07:56,000
now. “The future can wait. This moment can’t.” If you really could

145
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:59,167
see 10 seconds into the future… what would you use it for?
